# Lab-05 — Northbound. Copy this to `.env` and paste your keys.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # edit OPENAI_API_KEY below
#   make dev

OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional — web search (the UNVERIFIED tier). Two providers, two tools,
# gated independently: a tool whose key is absent is never registered, so the
# agent cannot reach a source it has no credential for. Neither key is
# required — without both, the verified catalogue is the agent's only source
# and every visa question escalates with nothing attached, which is a
# complete working configuration.
#
# Whichever provider runs, results are filtered by HOST against the allowlists
# in mcp_servers/northbound/sources.py before the agent sees them. A
# provider's own domain filter is a convenience; ours is the boundary.

# BRAVE — powers `research_visa_question`. Keyword search plus a page fetch,
# which suits government guidance: gov.uk is keyword-findable and serves
# plain HTML.
# Get a key: https://brave.com/search/api/
# BRAVE_API_KEY=BSA...

# EXA — powers `find_unverified_programmes`. Semantic search that returns the
# page TEXT with each result, so there is no separate fetch to be blocked.
# This is not a preference: Brave plus a fetch was tried here and failed.
# University course pages are JS-rendered and bot-protected, so the fetch
# returned an empty string and the agent was left naming courses off their
# titles. There is deliberately no Brave fallback for this tool.
# Get a key: https://dashboard.exa.ai/
# EXA_API_KEY=...

# Note: the agent reads its identity (id, name, model, role, workspace,
# confidence floor, web_search settings) from student_agent/agent-profile.yaml
# — not from env vars. Edit that file to reconfigure the agent. Credentials
# are the exception and live only here: the profile is committed, and
# load_profile refuses a key written into it.

# Supabase Postgres. Copy the connection string from your project's
# Settings → Database page and paste the password in place of the placeholder.
# Percent-encode the password if it contains @ : / ? # or %.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://postgres:PASSWORD@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require

# Clerk. The publishable key is public (it ships in the browser bundle); the
# secret key is not and must never leave this file.
# CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
